BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:"Skyward:" Anne Patterson & James Teschner
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTSTAMP:20260912T134358Z
UID:5bf21d2602dcd58d9e110b855238@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:"Skyward:" Anne Patterson &amp\; James Teschner Exhibition Dat
 es: September 5- October 3\, 2026 Opening Reception: Saturday September 5
 \, 2026\, 5:00- 7:00 PM "Skyward:" Anne Patterson &amp\; James Teschner Je
 ssica Hagen Fine Art + Design is pleased to announce the opening of "Skywa
 rd" featuring artists James Teschner and Anne Patterson on Saturday Septem
 ber 5\, 2026\, from 5:00- 7:00 PM. This exhibition showcases the paintings
  of James Teschner and the sculptural orbs of Anne Patterson. Teschner\, p
 ainting outdoors near his home in the remote farmlands of central France f
 ocuses on the setting sun\, the moon\, the sky\, and “those moments lead
 ing towards nightfall\, and the night itself\, whereby the landscape is ei
 ther being obliterated\, almost devoured by the sun’s all-consuming lumi
 nosity or being dissolved by the receding\, diminishing light.” Anne Pat
 terson is a multi-disciplinary artist based in Brooklyn. Working across pa
 inting\, sculpture\, and installation\, Patterson explores the ways our se
 nses overlap\, and how together they create an experience greater than the
  sum of its parts. Informed by her own synesthesia and her training as a s
 et designer\, she is often inspired by music and sound. Gallery owner Jess
 ica Hagen states\, “This is a magical exhibition. The radiance of James 
 Teschner’s oil paintings coalesce with the glow of Anne Patterson’s go
 ld-leafed orbs\, resulting in a sublime alchemy. It’s really a very spec
 ial show.” "Skyward" closes October 3\, 2026. Jessica Hagen Fine Art + D
 esign was founded in 2005 and features contemporary art including painting
 \, sculpture\, photography\, ceramics\, textiles\, and jewelry. Located in
  the historic Point section of Newport\, the gallery’s hours are Wednesd
 ay- Saturday 11:00 AM - 5:00 PM and Sunday 12:00- 5:00 PM. The gallery is 
 also open by appointment.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/even
 t/skyward%3a-anne-patterson-%26-james-teschner/111508/
LOCATION:Jessica Hagen Fine Art & Design\, 9A Bridge Street\, Newport\, RI
  02840
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/skyward%3a-anne-patterson-%26-j
 ames-teschner/111508/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:4th Annual Figmamma Farms Fig Festival
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTSTAMP:20260912T134358Z
UID:7233126c39966bc40c19d36942e4@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:4th Annual Figmamma Farms Fig Festival When: Saturday\, Septem
 ber 12th from 2:00 to 5:00 PM Where: 630 Puncatest Neck Road\, Tiverton\, 
 RI 02878 $5 suggested donation upon entrance Fig lovers from across New En
 gland are invite to gather for an afternoon celebrating one of the world's
  oldest cultivated fruits\, the fig at the 4th Annual @figmamma Farms Fig 
 Festival\, hosted by Firefly Figs in Tiverton\, R.I. Join in for a fun day
  of learning and networking on Saturday\, September 12th from 2:00 to 5:00
  PM. This family-friendly event offers a unique opportunity for experience
 d collectors\, backyard gardeners\, or curious fans to learn from passiona
 te and regional fig growers while connecting with other enthusiasts. Pre-r
 egistration opens August 8\, 2026.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland
 .com/event/4th-annual-figmamma-farms-fig-festival/111288/
LOCATION:630 Puncatest Neck Road\, 630 Puncatest Neck Road\, Tiverton\, RI
  02878 Time: 2:00 PM to 5:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/4th-annual-figmamma-farms-fig-f
 estival/111288/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Agon Challenge - Ancient Arcade and Charity Game Festival
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260912
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTSTAMP:20260912T134358Z
UID:fcf8c682787b26556e6e36252de9@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Join our 4th annual Ancient Greek themed pop-up arcade\, chari
 ty fundraiser\, and game festival. Enjoy live music\, games\, raffles\, ve
 ndors and being a part of the most EPIC toga party of the Common-Era! Fun 
 for the whole family! This festival is a free-play arcade of carnival game
 s\, party games\, board games\, card games\, and epic challenges! Many gam
 es have been reimagined to look as if they were made 2500 years ago. Manua
 l\, handcrafted\, and using little-to-no electricity. Have fun with our bo
 unce house\, scavenger hunt\, trivia\, and plenty of other fun family acti
 vities. Costume contest for best dressed! Togas encouraged\, but any famil
 y-appropriate costume is welcome. Game Tournament - Win the Agon Challenge
  tournament and be crowned a Heroes of Games\, receive a gold medal\, and 
 have the charity donation made in your honor! Proceeds of the night will b
 e donated to AIDS PROJECT RHODE ISLAND Adults $15 in advanced- $20 Day of.
  Kids $10 Learn More www.agonchallenge.com\n\nSource: https://www.visitrho
 deisland.com/event/agon-challenge-ancient-arcade-and-charity-game-festival
 /111210/
LOCATION:St. Anthony's Parish Center\, 25 Forest Ave.\, Pawtucket\, 02860 
 Time: 5:00 PM to 10:00 PM
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/agon-challenge-ancient-arcade-a
 nd-charity-game-festival/111210/
END:VEVENT
